contentText:
A hit song can be a gift and a curse. Yung Miami notched her first top 20 smash on the Billboard Hot 100 this summer with &#8220;Spend Dat,&#8221; and she parlayed the momentum garnered from the anthem leading into her debut solo album, Watch Dis , which arrived on Oct. 23 and debuted at No. 138 on the Billboard 200 .

Miami recently stopped by Billboard News for an interview with Tetris Kelly, talking all things surrounding the success of &#8220;Spend Dat&#8221; and her star-studded project, which included feeling the pressure of her first hit.

&#8220;Just seeing the success of &#8216;Spend Dat,&#8217; it gave me anxiety; I&#8217;m not gonna lie,&#8221; she admits. &#8220;I was excited, but I was like, &#8216;Damn, this is big.&#8217; I want this album to just be great, which I feel like it was. It really made me go back and hone in. Make sure that the album was top to bottom the way I needed it to be.&#8221;

Miami continues: &#8220;Before &#8216;Spend Dat,&#8217; I had a couple songs, and when I did &#8216;Spend Dat,&#8217; I was like, &#8216;Nah, I gotta go back in.&#8217; I think I know what the people want. I think I see the direction. After &#8216;Spend Dat,&#8217; I did &#8216;2008,&#8217; &#8216;F You&#8217; and the Bryson [Tiller] record came after.&#8221;

The 32-year-old didn&#8217;t hold back on the collaboration side, notching assists from G Herbo , Travis Scott, Bryson Tiller, Quavo, Rick Ross, Summer Walker and more. In the interview, she highlights teaming up with Walker and Bryson as a couple of her favorite moments on the album.

&#8220;I know doing this album, I wanted some big features, but Summer Walker, I love Summer Walker. I&#8217;m a Summer Walker girl,&#8221; she shares. &#8220;When it comes to R&B, that&#8217;s my No. 1 girl. I love every album she ever put out.&#8221;

Miami then gushes about Bryson: &#8220;Always been a fan of his; I love his music. I love the way he communicates to women. I just love his voice. I just think there&#8217;s something about him that&#8217;s just unique.&#8221;

As far as a potential City Girls reunion with JT, Miami had a one-word answer: &#8220;Inshallah.&#8221;

